# `GENRE-CONNECTOR-SPELLING`: `flowline` is the flowchart connector. Every rule that
# governed `edge` governs it unchanged — the operators, the [tail]/[mid]/[head]
# label positions, the option keys, the class join — because it is one scanner
# under three surface words and the model records a connector, not a spelling.
# 0.3 (`PAINT-ORDER-CONSTRUCT`): the last flowline also carried `plane=base`, and the key
# LEFT the language with the `plane` keyword — withdrawn, not renamed, so
# there is nothing to rewrite it to. It was incidental here (this fixture is
# about the connector, not about paint order), so the writing is deleted and
# `style=`/`class=` carry the option-key half of the claim on their own.
figdown 0.2 flowchart
title "Flowline is the connector"
class fail "Failure path" stroke=#dc2626
terminator start "Request received"
decision valid "Schema valid?"
process apply "Apply change"
node store "Audit store" shape=cylinder
terminator done "Response sent"
flowline start -> valid
flowline valid -[yes]-> apply
flowline valid -[no]-> store class=fail
flowline apply -> done
flowline store [copy] -- [kept] done style=dotted
flowline apply <-> store
